--- Returns a cosine value that fluctuates based on the current time
-- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/util.lua#L358-L363)
-- @param frequency --- The frequency of fluctuation
-- @param min --- Minimum value
-- @param max --- Maximum value
-- @param offset --- Offset variable that doesn't affect the rate of change, but causes the returned value to be offset by time
-- @return --- Cosine value
global function TimedCos(frequency: number, min: number, max: number, offset: number): number
end

--- Returns a sine value that fluctuates based on Global.CurTime. The value returned will be between the start value plus/minus the range value.
--- **BUG**: The range arguments don't work as intended. The existing (bugged) behavior is documented below.
-- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/util.lua#L351-L356)
-- @param frequency --- The frequency of fluctuation, in
-- @param origin --- The center value of the sine wave.
-- @param max --- This argument's distance from origin defines the size of the full range of the sine wave. For example, if origin is 3 and max is 5, then the full range of the sine wave is 5-3 = 2. 3 is the center point of the sine wave, so the sine wave will range between 2 and 4.
-- @param offset --- Offset variable that doesn't affect the rate of change, but causes the returned value to be offset by time
-- @return --- Sine value
global function TimedSin(frequency: number, origin: number, max: number, offset: number): number
end

--- Attempts to return an appropriate boolean for the given value
-- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/util.lua#L304-L310)
-- @param input --- The object to be converted to a boolean
-- @return --- * `false` for the boolean `false`.
--- * `false` for `"false"`.
--- * `false` for `"0"`.
--- * `false` for numeric `0`.
--- * `false` for `nil`.
--- * `true` otherwise.
global function tobool(input: any): boolean
end

--- Gets the associated type ID of the variable. Unlike Global.type, this does not work with no value - an argument must be provided.
--- **WARNING**: This will return `TYPE_TABLE` for Color objects.
--- All subclasses of Entity will return `TYPE_ENTITY`.
--- **BUG**: [This returns garbage for _LOADLIB objects.](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-requests/issues/1120
--- **BUG**: [This returns `TYPE_NIL` for protos.](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-requests/issues/1459
-- @param variable --- The variable to get the type ID of.
-- @return --- The type ID of the variable. See the Enums/TYPE.
global function TypeID(variable: any): number
end

--- This function takes a numeric indexed table and return all the members as a vararg. If specified, it will start at the given index and end at end index.
