--- GWEN is a system that allows you to load a spritesheet and generate a skin out of it.
global record GWEN
    --- This is a utility function that generates a specialized drawing function to render scalable textured borders. This is done with [9-slice scaling](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/9-slice_scaling). This is used in derma skins to create a bordered rectangle drawing function from an image.
    --- The texture is taken from `SKIN.GwenTexture` when the `material` argument is not supplied.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/derma/derma_gwen.lua#L6-L56)
    -- @param x --- The X coordinate on the texture.
    -- @param y --- The Y coordinate on the texture.
    -- @param w --- Width of the area on texture.
    -- @param h --- Height of the area on texture.
    -- @param left --- Left width of border.
    -- @param top --- Top width of border.
    -- @param right --- Right width of border.
    -- @param bottom --- Bottom width of border.
    -- @param material --- If set, given material will be used over the SKIN's default material, which is `SKIN.GwenTexture`.
    -- @return drawFunc --- The drawing function.
    --- <callback>
    --- <arg name="x" type="number">X coordinate for the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="y" type="number">Y coordinate for the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="w" type="number">Width of the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="h" type="number">Height of the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="clr" type="table" default="color_white">Optional color, default is white. Uses the Color.</arg>
    --- </callback>
    CreateTextureBorder: function(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, left: number, top: number, right: number, bottom: number, material: GIMaterial): function

    --- Used in derma skins to create a fixed scale rectangle drawing function from an image. it will be drawn in the center of the box.
    --- The texture is taken from `SKIN.GwenTexture` when the `material` is not supplied.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/derma/derma_gwen.lua#L87-L119)
    -- @param x --- The X coordinate on the texture.
    -- @param y --- The Y coordinate on the texture.
    -- @param w --- Width of the area on texture.
    -- @param h --- Height of the area on texture.
    -- @param material --- If set, given material will be used over the SKIN's default material, which is `SKIN.GwenTexture`.
    -- @return --- The drawing function.
    --- <callback>
    --- <arg name="x" type="number">X coordinate for the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="y" type="number">Y coordinate for the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="w" type="number">Width of the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="h" type="number">Height of the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="clr" type="table" default="color_white">Optional color, default is white. Uses the Color.</arg>
    --- </callback>
    CreateTextureCentered: function(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, material: GIMaterial): function

    --- Helper function that returns a specialized drawing function for rendering a texture that scales freely to fit the given area.
    --- The texture is taken from `SKIN.GwenTexture` when the `material` is not supplied.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/derma/derma_gwen.lua#L58-L85)
    -- @param x --- The X coordinate on the texture.
    -- @param y --- The Y coordinate on the texture.
    -- @param w --- Width of the area on texture.
    -- @param h --- Height of the area on texture.
    -- @param material --- If set, given material will be used over the SKIN's default material, which is `SKIN.GwenTexture`.
    -- @return --- The drawing function.
    --- <callback>
    --- <arg name="x" type="number">X coordinate for the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="y" type="number">Y coordinate for the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="w" type="number">Width of the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="h" type="number">Height of the box.</arg>
    --- <arg name="clr" type="table" default="color_white">Optional color, default is white. Uses the Color.</arg>
    --- </callback>
    CreateTextureNormal: function(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, material: GIMaterial): function

    --- Retrieves the color from a materials texture at the provided UV coordinates
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/derma/derma_gwen.lua#L121-L127)
    -- @param x --- X position of the pixel to get the color from.
    -- @param y --- Y position of the pixel to get the color from.
    -- @return --- The color of the point on the skin as a Color.
    TextureColor: function(x: number, y: number): table
end


--- This library is used internally by Garry's Mod to help keep track of achievement progress and unlock the appropriate achievements once a certain number is reached.
global record achievements
    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of balloons burst. Once this count reaches 1000, the 'Popper' achievement is unlocked.
    BalloonPopped: function()

    --- Returns the amount of achievements in Garry's Mod.
    -- @return --- The amount of achievements available.
    Count: function(): number

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of balls eaten. Once this count reaches 200, the 'Ball Eater' achievement is unlocked.
    EatBall: function()

    --- Retrieves progress of given achievement.
    -- @param achievementID --- The ID of achievement to retrieve progress of. Note: IDs start from 0, not 1.
    GetCount: function(achievementID: number)

    --- Retrieves description of given achievement.
    -- @param achievementID --- The ID of achievement to retrieve description of. Note: IDs start from 0, not 1.
    -- @return --- Description of an achievement.
    GetDesc: function(achievementID: number): string

    --- Retrieves progress goal of given achievement.
    -- @param achievementID --- The ID of achievement to retrieve goal of. Note: IDs start from 0, not 1.
    -- @return --- Progress goal of an achievement.
    GetGoal: function(achievementID: number): number

    --- Retrieves name of given achievement.
    -- @param achievementID --- The ID of achievement to retrieve name of. Note: IDs start from 0, not 1.
    -- @return --- Name of an achievement.
    GetName: function(achievementID: number): string

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of baddies killed. Once this count reaches 1000, the 'War Zone' achievement is unlocked.
    IncBaddies: function()

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of innocent animals killed. Once this count reaches 1000, the 'Innocent Bystander' achievement is unlocked.
    IncBystander: function()

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of friendly NPCs killed. Once this count reaches 1000, the 'Bad Friend' achievement is unlocked.
    IncGoodies: function()

    --- Used in GMod 12 in the achievements menu to show the user if they have unlocked certain achievements.
    -- @param AchievementID --- Internal Achievement ID number.
    -- @return --- Returns true if the given achievementID is achieved.
    IsAchieved: function(AchievementID: number): boolean

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of things removed. Once this count reaches 5000, the 'Destroyer' achievement is unlocked.
    Remover: function()

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of how many times the spawnmenu has been opened. Once this count reaches 100,000, the 'Menu User' achievement is unlocked.
    SpawnMenuOpen: function()

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of NPCs spawned. Once this count reaches 1000, the 'Procreator' achievement is unlocked.
    SpawnedNPC: function()

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of props spawned. Once this count reaches 5000, the 'Creator' achievement is unlocked.
    SpawnedProp: function()

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Adds one to the count of ragdolls spawned. Once this count reaches 2000, the 'Dollhouse' achievement is unlocked.
    SpawnedRagdoll: function()
end


--- The ai library.
global record ai
    --- Returns the number of AI nodes on the map, used by the base game NPCs.
    --- For nextbots, see navmesh.
    -- @return --- The node count.
    GetNodeCount: function(): number

    --- Translates a schedule name to its corresponding ID.
    -- @param sched --- Then schedule name. In most cases, this will be the same as the Enums/SCHED name.
    -- @return --- The schedule ID, see Enums/SCHED. Returns -1 if the schedule name isn't valid.
    GetScheduleID: function(sched: string): number

    --- Returns the squad leader of the given squad.
    -- @param squad --- The squad name.
    -- @return --- The squad leader.
    GetSquadLeader: function(squad: string): GNPC

    --- Returns the amount of members a given squad has. See also ai.GetSquadMembers.
    -- @param squad --- The squad name.
    -- @return --- The member count.
    GetSquadMemberCount: function(squad: string): number

    --- Returns all members of a given squad. See also ai.GetSquadMemberCount and NPC:GetSquad.
    -- @param squad --- The squad name.
    -- @return --- A table of NPCs in the given squad.
    GetSquadMembers: function(squad: string): table

    --- Translates a task name to its corresponding ID.
    -- @param task --- The task name.
    -- @return --- The task ID, see [ai_task.h](https://github.com/ValveSoftware/source-sdk-2013/blob/55ed12f8d1eb6887d348be03aee5573d44177ffb/mp/src/game/server/ai_task.h#L89-L502). Returns -1 if the schedule name isn't valid.
    GetTaskID: function(task: string): number
end


--- Allows you to set up a schedule for NPCs to follow. This lets you dictate their actions.
global record ai_schedule
    --- Creates a schedule for scripted NPC.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/ai_schedule.lua#L89-L98)
    -- @param name --- Name of the schedule.
    -- @return --- A table containing schedule information to be used with ENTITY:StartSchedule.
    New: function(name: string): table
end


--- Used to create tasks for scripted NPCs.
global record ai_task
    --- Create a new empty task. Used by Schedule:AddTask and Schedule:EngTask.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/ai_task.lua#L109-L123)
    -- @return --- The new task object.
    New: function(): GTask
end


--- The baseclass library. Used to lookup a field from a metatable.
global record baseclass
    --- Gets the base class of an an object.
    --- This is used not just by entities, but also by widgets, panels, drive modes, weapons and gamemodes (with "gamemode_" prefix).
    --- The keyword **DEFINE_BASECLASS** translates into a call to this function. In the engine, it is replaced with:
    --- ```lua
    --- local BaseClass = baseclass.Get
    --- ```
    --- **NOTE**: You should prefer using this instead of `self.BaseClass` to avoid infinite recursion.
    --- For more information, including usage examples, see the BaseClasses reference page.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/baseclass.lua#L32-L41)
    -- @param name --- The child class.
    -- @return --- The base class's meta table.
    Get: function(name: string): table

    --- Add a new base class that can be derived by others. This is done automatically for:
    --- * [panels](vgui.Register)
    --- * [drive modes](drive.Register)
    --- * [entities and widgets](scripted_ents.Register)
    --- * [weapons](weapons.Register)
    --- * [gamemodes](gamemode.Register) (with prefix "gamemode_")
    --- For more information, including usage examples, see the BaseClasses reference page.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/baseclass.lua#L43-L58)
    -- @param name --- The name of this base class. Must be completely unique.
    -- @param tab --- The base class.
    Set: function(name: string, tab: table)
end


--- The bitwise library contains useful functions for bitwise operations.
--- Make sure you're familiar with [Bitwise Operators](https://code.tutsplus.com/articles/understanding-bitwise-operators--active-11301)
global record bit
    --- Returns the arithmetically shifted value.
    -- @param value --- The value to be manipulated.
    -- @param shiftCount --- Amounts of bits to shift.
    -- @return --- The shifted value.
    arshift: function(value: number, shiftCount: number): number

    --- Performs the bitwise `and` for all values specified.
    -- @param value --- The value to be manipulated.
    -- @param ... --- Values bit to perform bitwise "and" with. Optional.
    -- @return --- Result of bitwise "and" operation.
    band: function(value: number, ...: any): number

    --- Returns the bitwise not of the value. Inverts every bit of the 32bit integer.
    -- @param value --- The value to be inverted.
    -- @return --- The result of bitwise not. 0101 becomes 1010, etc.
    bnot: function(value: number): number

    --- Returns the bitwise OR of all values specified.
    -- @param value1 --- The first value.
    -- @param ... --- Extra values to be evaluated. (must all be numbers)
    -- @return --- The bitwise OR result between all numbers.
    bor: function(value1: number, ...: any): number

    --- Swaps the byte order.
    -- @param value --- The value to be byte swapped.
    -- @return --- The resulting swapped value.
    bswap: function(value: number): number

    --- Returns the bitwise xor of all values specified.
    -- @param value --- The value to be manipulated.
    -- @param otherValues --- Values bit xor with. Optional.
    -- @return --- The XORed value.
    bxor: function(value: number, otherValues: number): number

    --- Returns the result of shifting given value left bitwise by given number of bits. See [this wiki article](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#Bit_shifts) for more details.
    --- **NOTE**: The returned value will be clamped to a signed 32-bit integer, even on 64-bit builds.
    -- @param value --- The value to be manipulated.
    -- @param shiftCount --- Amounts of bits to shift left by.
    -- @return --- The resulting value. Input of `0b1001` will become `0b10010` for one left shift, etc.
    lshift: function(value: number, shiftCount: number): number

    --- Returns the left rotated value.
    -- @param value --- The value to be manipulated.
    -- @param shiftCount --- Amounts of bits to rotate left by.
    -- @return --- The shifted value.
    rol: function(value: number, shiftCount: number): number

    --- Returns the right rotated value.
    -- @param value --- The value to be manipulated.
    -- @param shiftCount --- Amounts of bits to rotate right by.
    -- @return --- The shifted value.
    ror: function(value: number, shiftCount: number): number

    --- Returns the right shifted value.
    --- **NOTE**: The returned value will be clamped to a signed 32-bit integer, even on 64-bit builds.
    -- @param value --- The value to be manipulated.
    -- @param shiftCount --- Amounts of bits to shift right by.
    -- @return --- The shifted value.
    rshift: function(value: number, shiftCount: number): number

    --- Normalizes the specified value and clamps it in the range of a signed 32bit integer.
    -- @param value --- The value to be normalized.
    -- @return --- The 32 bits of the provided value.
    tobit: function(value: number): number

    --- Returns the hexadecimal representation of the number with the specified number of characters.
    -- @param value --- The value to be normalized.
    -- @param characters --- Maximum number of characters, if set. The absolute maximum is 8.
    -- @return --- The hexadecimal representation, such as "00000001".
    tohex: function(value: number, characters: number): string
end


--- This directs all drawing to be done to a certain 2D or 3D plane or position, until the corresponding "End" function is called.
--- The matrix functions exist, but are mostly unusable unless you're familiar with the source engine's layout for each aspect.
global record cam
    --- Shakes the screen at a certain position.
    -- @param pos --- Origin of the shake.
    -- @param angles --- Angles of the shake.
    -- @param factor --- The shake factor.
    ApplyShake: function(pos: GVector, angles: GAngle, factor: number)

    --- Switches the renderer back to the previous drawing mode from a 3D context.
    --- This function is an alias of cam.End3D.
    End: function()

    --- Switches the renderer back to the previous drawing mode from a 2D context.
    End2D: function()

    --- Switches the renderer back to the previous drawing mode from a 3D context.
    End3D: function()

    --- Switches the renderer back to the previous drawing mode from a 3D2D context.
    End3D2D: function()

    --- Switches the renderer back to the previous drawing mode from a 3D orthographic rendering context.
    EndOrthoView: function()

    --- Returns a copy of the model matrix that is at the top of the stack.
    --- **NOTE**: Editing the matrix **will not** edit the current view. To do so, you will have to use cam.PushModelMatrix.
    -- @return --- The currently active matrix.
    GetModelMatrix: function(): GVMatrix

    --- Tells the renderer to ignore the depth buffer and draw any upcoming operation "ontop" of everything that was drawn yet.
    --- This is identical to calling `render.DepthRange( 0, 0.01 )` for `true` and  `render.DepthRange( 0, 1 )` for `false`. See render.DepthRange.
    -- @param ignoreZ --- Determines whenever to ignore the depth buffer or not.
    IgnoreZ: function(ignoreZ: boolean)

    --- Pops the current active rendering matrix from the stack and reinstates the previous one.
    PopModelMatrix: function()

    --- Pushes the specified matrix onto the render matrix stack. Unlike opengl, this will replace the current model matrix.
    --- **NOTE**: This does not work with cam.Start3D2D if `multiply` is false.
    --- **WARNING**: When used in the Paint function of a panel, if you want to rely on the top-left position of the panel, you must use VMatrix:Translate with the (0, 0) position of the panel relative to the screen.
    -- @param matrix --- The matrix to push.
    -- @param multiply --- If set, multiplies given matrix with currently active matrix (cam.GetModelMatrix) before pushing.
    PushModelMatrix: function(matrix: GVMatrix, multiply: boolean)

    --- Sets up a new rendering context. This is an extended version of cam.Start3D and cam.Start2D. Must be finished by cam.End3D or cam.End2D.
    --- **BUG**: [This will not update current view properties for 3D contexts.](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/2682
    -- @param dataTbl --- Render context config. See Structures/RenderCamData.
    Start: function(dataTbl: table)

    --- Sets up a new 2D rendering context. Must be finished by cam.End2D.
    --- This is almost always used with a render target from the render. To set its position use render.SetViewPort with a target already stored.
    --- **NOTE**: This will put an identity matrix at the top of the model matrix stack. If you are trying to use cam.PushModelMatrix, call it after this function and not before.
    --- **NOTE**: Provides a 2D rendering context
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/extensions/client/render.lua#L109-L113)
    Start2D: function()

    --- Sets up a new 3D rendering context. Must be finished by cam.End3D.
    --- For more advanced settings such as an orthographic view, use cam.Start instead, which this is an alias of basically.
    --- All parameters are optional, and fall back parameters that of the "current" or "last" render operation.
    --- **NOTE**: Provides a 3D rendering context
    --- **BUG**: [Negative x/y values won't work.](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/1995
    --- **BUG**: [This will not update current view properties.](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/2682
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/extensions/client/render.lua#L115-L144)
    -- @param pos --- Render cam position.
    -- @param angles --- Render cam angles.
    -- @param fov --- Field of view.
    -- @param x --- X coordinate of where to start the new view port.
    -- @param y --- Y coordinate of where to start the new view port.
    -- @param w --- Width of the new viewport.
    -- @param h --- Height of the new viewport.
    -- @param zNear --- Distance to near clipping plane.
    --- **NOTE**: Both `zNear` and `zFar` need a value before any of them work.
    --- zNear also requires a value higher than 0.
    -- @param zFar --- Distance to far clipping plane.
    Start3D: function(pos: GVector, angles: GAngle, fov: number, x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, zNear: number, zFar: number)

    --- Sets up the model transformation matrix to draw 2D content in 3D space and pushes it into the stack (cam.PushModelMatrix).
    --- Matrix formula:
    --- ```
    --- local m = Matrix()
    --- m:SetAngles( angles )
    --- m:SetTranslation( pos )
    --- m:SetScale( Vector( scale, -scale, 1 ) )
    --- ```
    --- **WARNING**: This must be closed by cam.End3D2D. If not done so, unexpected issues might arise.
    --- render.SetToneMappingScaleLinear may of use when dealing with bloom.
    -- @param pos --- Origin of the 3D2D context, ie. the top left corner, (0, 0).
    -- @param angles --- Angles of the 3D2D context.
    --- +x in the 2d context corresponds to +x of the angle (its forward direction).
    --- +y in the 2d context corresponds to -y of the angle (its right direction).
    --- If (dx, dy) are your desired (+x, +y) unit vectors, the angle you want is dx:AngleEx(dx:Cross(-dy)).
    -- @param scale --- The scale of the render context.
    --- If scale is 1 then 1 pixel in 2D context will equal to 1 unit in 3D context.
    Start3D2D: function(pos: GVector, angles: GAngle, scale: number)

    --- Sets up a new 3d context using orthographic projection.
    -- @param leftOffset --- The left plane offset.
    -- @param topOffset --- The top plane offset.
    -- @param rightOffset --- The right plane offset.
    -- @param bottomOffset --- The bottom plane offset.
    StartOrthoView: function(leftOffset: number, topOffset: number, rightOffset: number, bottomOffset: number)
end


--- The chat library's purpose is to interface with the default chatbox.
global record chat
    --- Adds text to the local player's chat box (which only they can read).
    -- @param arguments --- The arguments. Arguments can be:
    --- * table - Color. Will set the color for all following strings until the next Color argument.
    --- * string - Text to be added to the chat box.
    --- * Player - Adds the name of the player in the player's team color to the chat box.
    --- * any - Any other type, such as Entity will be converted to string and added as text.
    AddText: function(...: any)

    --- Closes the chat window.
    Close: function()

    --- Returns the chatbox position.
    -- @return --- The X coordinate of the chatbox's position.
    -- @return --- The Y coordinate of the chatbox's position.
    GetChatBoxPos: function(): number, number

    --- Returns the chatbox size.
    -- @return --- The width of the chatbox.
    -- @return --- The height of the chatbox.
    GetChatBoxSize: function(): number, number

    --- Opens the chat window.
    -- @param mode --- If equals 1, opens public chat, otherwise opens team chat.
    Open: function(mode: number)

    --- Plays the chat "tick" sound.
    PlaySound: function()
end


--- The cleanup library allows you to control what happens to custom entities when the clean-up buttons are pressed in the Utilities tab of the Spawn menu (default Q).
global record cleanup
    --- Adds an entity to a player's cleanup list.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L59-L74)
    -- @param pl --- Who's cleanup list to add the entity to.
    -- @param type --- The type of cleanup.
    -- @param ent --- The entity to add to the player's cleanup list.
    Add: function(pl: GPlayer, type: string, ent: GEntity)

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    ---  Called by the `gmod_admin_cleanup` console command. Allows admins to clean up the server.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L148-L200)
    -- @param pl --- The player that called the console command.
    -- @param command --- The console command that called this function.
    -- @param args --- First and only arg is the cleanup type.
    CC_AdminCleanup: function(pl: GPlayer, command: string, args: table)

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    ---  Called by the `gmod_cleanup` console command. Allows players to cleanup their own props.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L98-L146)
    -- @param pl --- The player that called the console command.
    -- @param command --- The console command that called this function.
    -- @param args --- First and only argument is the cleanup type.
    CC_Cleanup: function(pl: GPlayer, command: string, args: table)

    --- Gets the cleanup list.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L40-L42)
    GetList: function()

    --- Gets the table of cleanup types.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L31-L33)
    -- @return --- A list of cleanup types.
    GetTable: function(): table

    --- Registers a new cleanup type.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L17-L29)
    -- @param type --- Name of type.
    Register: function(type: string)

    --- Replaces one entity in the cleanup module with another.
    --- You very likely want to call undo.ReplaceEntity with the same entities as well.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L76-L95)
    -- @param from --- The old entity.
    -- @param to --- The new entity. Can be a `NULL` entity to remove the old entity from the cleanup system.
    -- @return --- Whether any action was taken.
    ReplaceEntity: function(from: GEntity, to: GEntity): boolean

    --- Repopulates the clients cleanup menu.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/cleanup.lua#L207-L238)
    UpdateUI: function()
end


--- The concommand library is used to create console commands which can be used to network (basic) information & events between the client and the server.
global record concommand
    --- Creates a console command that runs a function in lua with optional autocompletion function and help text.
    --- **WARNING**: Clients can still run commands created only on the server. Always check permissions in the callback.
    --- **BUG**: [This will fail if the concommand was previously removed with concommand.Remove in a different realm (creating a command on the client that was removed from the server and vice-versa).](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/1183
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/concommand.lua#L24-L33)
    -- @param name --- The command name to be used in console.
    --- This cannot be a name of existing console command or console variable. It will silently fail if it is.
    -- @param callback --- The function to run when the concommand is executed.
    --- <callback>
    --- <arg name="ply" type="Player">The player that ran the concommand. NULL entity if command was entered with the dedicated server console.</arg>
    --- <arg name="cmd" type="string">The concommand string (if one callback is used for several concommands).</arg>
    --- <arg name="args" type="table">A table of all string arguments.</arg>
    --- <arg name="argStr" type="string">The arguments as a string (including double quotes if there were any).</arg>
    --- </callback>
    -- @param autoComplete --- The function to call which should return a table of options for autocompletion. (Autocompletion Tutorial)
    --- This only properly works on the client since it is **not** networked.
    --- <callback>
    --- <arg name="cmd" type="string">The concommand this autocompletion is for.</arg>
    --- <arg name="argStr" type="string">The arguments typed so far.</arg>
    --- <arg name="args" type="table">A table of all string arguments.</arg>
    --- <ret name="tbl" type="table">A table containing the autocomplete options to display.</ret>
    --- </callback>
    -- @param helpText --- The text to display should a user run 'help cmdName'.
    -- @param flags --- Console command modifier flags. Either a bitflag, or a table of enums. See Enums/FCVAR.
    Add: function(name: string, callback: function, autoComplete: function, helpText: string, flags: E_FCVAR|{number})

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    ---  Used by the engine to call the autocomplete function for a console command, and retrieve returned options.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/concommand.lua#L63-L75)
    -- @param command --- Name of command.
    -- @param arguments --- Arguments given to the command.
    -- @return --- Possibilities for auto-completion. This is the return value of the auto-complete callback.
    AutoComplete: function(command: string, arguments: string): table

    --- Returns the tables of all console command callbacks, and autocomplete functions, that were added to the game with concommand.Add.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/concommand.lua#L16-L22)
    -- @return --- Table of command callback functions.
    -- @return --- Table of command autocomplete functions.
    GetTable: function(): {string:function}, {string:function}

    --- Removes a console command.
    --- **BUG**: [concommand.Add will fail if the concommand was previously removed with this function in a different realm (creating a command on the client that was removed from the server and vice-versa).](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod-issues/issues/1183
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/concommand.lua#L35-L43)
    -- @param name --- The name of the command to be removed.
    Remove: function(name: string)

    --- **INTERNAL**: You might be looking for Global.RunConsoleCommand or Player:ConCommand.
    --- Used by the engine to run a console command's callback function. This will only be called for commands that were added with Global.AddConsoleCommand, which concommand.Add calls internally. An error is sent to the player's console if no callback is found.
    --- This will still be called for concommands removed with concommand.Remove but will return false. This will not be called for concommands added by the engine, only those made from Lua.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/concommand.lua#L45-L61)
    -- @param ply --- Player to run concommand on.
    -- @param cmd --- Command name.
    -- @param args --- Command arguments.
    --- Can be table or string.
    -- @param argumentString --- string of all arguments sent to the command.
    -- @return --- `true` if the console command with the given name exists, and `false` if it doesn't.
    Run: function(ply: GPlayer, cmd: string, args: any, argumentString: string): boolean
end


--- The constraint library allows you to control the constraint system built into the physics engine (rope, weld, ballsockets, etc).
global record constraint
    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Stores the constraint entity in the constrained entity's `Constraints` table.
    --- This will make the `constrt` entity be removed if any of the other entities `ent1`, `ent2`, `ent3` or `ent4` are removed by any means.
    --- To prevent this, constraint.AddConstraintTableNoDelete can be used instead.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/constraint.lua#L352-L368)
    -- @param ent1 --- The entity to store the information on.
    -- @param constrt --- The constraint to store in the entity's table.
    -- @param ent2 --- Optional. If different from `ent1`, the info will also be stored in the table for this entity.
    -- @param ent3 --- Optional. Same as `ent2`.
    -- @param ent4 --- Optional. Same as `ent2`.
    AddConstraintTable: function(ent1: GEntity, constrt: GEntity, ent2: GEntity, ent3: GEntity, ent4: GEntity)

    --- **INTERNAL**:
    --- Stores info about the constraints on the entity's table.
    --- The only difference between this and constraint.AddConstraintTable is that the constraint does not get deleted when any of the constrained entities are removed.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/constraint.lua#L374-L389)
    -- @param ent1 --- The entity to store the information on.
    -- @param constrt --- The constraint to store in the entity's table.
    -- @param ent2 --- Optional. If different from `ent1`, the info will also be stored in the table for this entity.
    -- @param ent3 --- Optional. Same as `ent2`.
    -- @param ent4 --- Optional. Same as `ent2`.
    AddConstraintTableNoDelete: function(ent1: GEntity, constrt: GEntity, ent2: GEntity, ent3: GEntity, ent4: GEntity)

    --- Creates an advanced ballsocket (ragdoll) constraint. See constraint.Ballsocket for the simpler version.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/constraint.lua#L837-L906)
    -- @param ent1 --- First entity.
    -- @param ent2 --- Second entity.
    -- @param bone1 --- PhysObj number of first entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param bone2 --- PhysObj number of second entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param localPos1 --- Position relative to the the first physics object to constrain to.
    -- @param localPos2 --- Position relative to the the second physics object to constrain to.
    --- **WARNING**: Does nothing!
    -- @param forceLimit --- Amount of force until it breaks (0 = unbreakable).
    -- @param torqueLimit --- Amount of torque (rotation speed) until it breaks (0 = unbreakable).
    -- @param xMin --- Minimum angle in rotations around the X axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param yMin --- Minimum angle in rotations around the Y axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param zMin --- Minimum angle in rotations around the Z axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param xMax --- Maximum angle in rotations around the X axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param yMax --- Maximum angle in rotations around the Y axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param zMax --- Maximum angle in rotations around the Z axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param xFric --- Rotational friction in the X axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param yFric --- Rotational friction in the Y axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param zFric --- Rotational friction in the Z axis local to the constraint.
    -- @param onlyRotation --- Only limit rotation, free movement.
    -- @param noCollide --- Whether the entities should be no-collided.
    -- @return --- A [phys_ragdollconstraint](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Phys_ragdollconstraint) entity. Will return `false` if the constraint could not be created.
    AdvBallsocket: function(ent1: GEntity, ent2: GEntity, bone1: number, bone2: number, localPos1: GVector, localPos2: GVector, forceLimit: number, torqueLimit: number, xMin: number, yMin: number, zMin: number, xMax: number, yMax: number, zMax: number, xFric: number, yFric: number, zFric: number, onlyRotation: number, noCollide: number): GEntity

    --- Creates an axis constraint.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/constraint.lua#L773-L830)
    -- @param ent1 --- First entity.
    -- @param ent2 --- Second entity.
    -- @param bone1 --- PhysObj number of first entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param bone2 --- PhysObj number of second entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param localPos1 --- Position relative to the the first physics object to constrain to.
    -- @param localPos2 --- Position relative to the the second physics object to constrain to.
    -- @param forceLimit --- Amount of force until it breaks (0 = unbreakable).
    -- @param torqueLimit --- Amount of torque (rotational force) until it breaks (0 = unbreakable).
    -- @param friction --- Constraint friction.
    -- @param noCollide --- Whether the entities should be no-collided.
    -- @param localAxis --- If you include the LocalAxis then LPos2 will not be used in the final constraint. However, LPos2 is still a required argument.
    -- @param dontAddTable --- Whether or not to add the constraint info on the entity table. See constraint.AddConstraintTable.
    -- @return --- The created constraint. ([phys_hinge](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Phys_hinge)) Will return `false` if the constraint could not be created.
    Axis: function(ent1: GEntity, ent2: GEntity, bone1: number, bone2: number, localPos1: GVector, localPos2: GVector, forceLimit: number, torqueLimit: number, friction: number, noCollide: number, localAxis: GVector, dontAddTable: boolean): GEntity

    --- Creates a ballsocket joint. See See constraint.AdvBallsocket if you also wish to limit rotation angles in some way.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/constraint.lua#L1214-L1258)
    -- @param ent1 --- First entity.
    -- @param ent2 --- Second entity.
    -- @param bone1 --- PhysObj number of first entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param bone2 --- PhysObj number of second entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param localPos --- Center position of the joint, relative to the **second** entity's physics object.
    -- @param forceLimit --- Amount of force until it breaks (0 = unbreakable).
    -- @param torqueLimit --- Amount of torque (rotational force) until it breaks (0 = unbreakable).
    -- @param nocollide --- Whether the constrained entities should collided with each other or not.
    -- @return --- The created constraint. ([phys_ballsocket](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Phys_ballsocket)) Will return `false` if the constraint could not be created.
    Ballsocket: function(ent1: GEntity, ent2: GEntity, bone1: number, bone2: number, localPos: GVector, forceLimit: number, torqueLimit: number, nocollide: number): GEntity

    --- Basic checks to make sure that the specified entity and bone are valid. Returns false if we should not be constraining the entity.
