    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param ent2 --- Second entity.
    -- @param localPos2 --- Position relative to the the second physics object to constrain to.
    -- @param bone2 --- PhysObj number of second entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param keyValues --- Any additional key/values to be set on the rope.
    -- @return --- The created rope ([keyframe_rope](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Keyframe_rope)), or `nil` or failure.
    CreateKeyframeRope: function(pos: GVector, width: number, material: string, constraint: GEntity, ent1: GEntity, localPos1: GVector, bone1: number, ent2: GEntity, localPos2: GVector, bone2: number, keyValues: table): GEntity

    --- Creates an invisible, non-moveable anchor point in the world to which things can be attached.
    --- **NOTE**: The entity used internally by this function (`gmod_anchor`) only exists in Sandbox derived gamemodes, meaning this function will only work in these gamemodes.
    --- To use this in other gamemodes, you may need to create your own [gmod_anchor](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/gamemodes/sandbox/entities/entities/gmod_anchor.lua) entity.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/constraint.lua#L665-L677)
    -- @param pos --- The position to spawn the anchor at
    -- @return --- The anchor entity. (`gmod_anchor`)
    -- @return --- The achor entity's physics object. (Entity:GetPhysicsObject)
    -- @return --- Always `0`.
    -- @return --- Always `vector_zero`.
    CreateStaticAnchorPoint: function(pos: GVector): GEntity, GPhysObj, number, GVector

    --- Creates an elastic rope constraint.
    -- [View source](https://github.com/Facepunch/garrysmod/blob/master/garrysmod/lua/includes/modules/constraint.lua#L546-L614)
    -- @param ent1 --- First entity.
    -- @param ent2 --- Second entity.
    -- @param bone1 --- PhysObj number of first entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls).
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param bone2 --- PhysObj number of second entity to constrain to. (0 for non-ragdolls). Must be different from `bone1`.
    --- See Entity:TranslateBoneToPhysBone.
    -- @param localPos1 --- Position relative to the the first physics object to constrain to.
    -- @param localPos2 --- Position relative to the the second physics object to constrain to.
    -- @param constant --- Stiffness of the elastic. The larger the number the less the elastic will stretch.
    -- @param damping --- How much energy the elastic loses. The larger the number, the less bouncy the elastic.
    -- @param relDamping --- The amount of energy the elastic loses proportional to the relative velocity of the two objects the elastic is attached to.
    -- @param material --- The material of the rope. If unset, will be solid black.
    -- @param width --- Width of rope.
    -- @param stretchOnly --- Apply physics forces only on stretch.
    -- @param color --- The color of the rope. See Global.Color.
    -- @return --- The created constraint. ([phys_spring](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Phys_spring)) Will return `false` if the constraint could not be created.
    -- @return --- The created rope. ([keyframe_rope](https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Keyframe_rope)) Will return `nil` if the constraint could not be created.
    Elastic: function(ent1: GEntity, ent2: GEntity, bone1: number, bone2: number, localPos1: GVector, localPos2: GVector, constant: number, damping: number, relDamping: number, material: string, width: number, stretchOnly: boolean, color: table): GEntity, GEntity

    --- Returns the constraint of a specified type between two entities, if it exists
